# CaramOS: which apps open office documents. The same list is x-cinnamon-mimeapps.list (Cinnamon edition) and
# xfce-mimeapps.list (Xfce edition), from DEFAULTS in /usr/share/caramos-ota/open-document/caramos_open_document.py
# (caramos-ota); a test keeps the three the same.
#
# CaramOS comes without an office suite: the App Center offers ONLYOFFICE, WPS Office and LibreOffice. Each list
# names those suites first, so the first one installed opens the file. When none is,
# caramos-open-document.desktop opens the file with another app that opens it, or suggests the App Center.
# Without these lists, .docx, .xlsx, .pptx and OpenDocument files, which are zip files, went to the app of
# application/zip.
#
# These are the system's defaults for each desktop (XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP X-Cinnamon or XFCE), read before Linux
# Mint's /usr/share/applications/mimeapps.list. A choice made elsewhere comes first: the user's own (Open With, Set
# as default: ~/.config/mimeapps.list), or an administrator's in /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list. CaramOS 1.4.0 and 1.5.0
# had this list in /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list, a configuration file of the package: on a computer that already had that
# file, dpkg asked which one to keep, nobody could answer, and the update stopped (ticket H-1207).
[Default Applications]
